1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,000
Hi, we are team Polaris Window.

2
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:05,000
Landing at the Moon's south pole means fighting for sunlight and a line of sight to Earth.

3
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:08,500
Polaris Window: know exactly when and where to land.

4
00:00:08,500 --> 00:00:14,000
Built on NASA LOLA terrain and JPL ephemeris: stand at any site and watch the Sun and Earth cross the real horizon.

5
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:19,000
Enter your mission length and power and comms limits, and it ranks the best landing dates.

6
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:23,000
Map sunlight, Earth contact and safe flat ground across the whole region...

7
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:26,000
...and every result is checked against NASA's own illumination maps and JPL Horizons.

8
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:30,000
From mission planners to classrooms: pick your window to the Moon.
